* OPA365 behavioral macro-model (NOT the TI SPICE model)
*
* Pins : inp, inn, out, vdd, gnd
* Single dominant pole (gain-bandwidth), slew limit, rail-to-rail clamp with
* headroom, open-loop output resistance, input offset / bias current /
* input capacitances.
*
* Global .param values used (set by build_model.py from config.json):
*   op_gbw, op_aol, op_sr, op_vos, op_ib, op_cdiff, op_ccm, op_ro, op_vmargin
.param op_gm=1m
.param op_c1={op_gm/(6.283185307*op_gbw)}
.subckt OPA365_BEH inp inn out vdd gnd
Ccmp inp gnd {op_ccm}
Ccmn inn gnd {op_ccm}
Cdif inp inn {op_cdiff}
Ibp  inp gnd {op_ib}
Ibn  inn gnd {op_ib}
Bgm  gnd int I=limit({op_gm}*(V(inp)-V(inn)+{op_vos}), -{op_sr}*{op_c1}, {op_sr}*{op_c1})
Rint int gnd {op_aol/op_gm}
Cint int gnd {op_c1}
Bout outi gnd V=limit(V(int), V(gnd)+{op_vmargin}, V(vdd)-{op_vmargin})
Ro   outi out {op_ro}
.ends OPA365_BEH
